WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.290
Reporting completes the workflow by delivering the answer in a form the intended audience

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:05.275
can use.

00:00:05.275 --> 00:00:07.295
Start with the requirement and decision context.

00:00:07.295 --> 00:00:10.360
The report should make the main finding, confidence, significance,

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.800
and recommended next step easy to identify.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.751
An executive summary should be concise without hiding uncertainty.

00:00:15.751 --> 00:00:19.090
Supporting sections can provide a timeline, relationship map, source notes,

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:20.960
and analytical rationale.

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:24.050
Technical readers may need detailed public indicators or infrastructure context,

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:26.717
while leaders may need implications and options.

00:00:26.717 --> 00:00:29.074
Cite evidence close to the claim it supports.

00:00:29.074 --> 00:00:32.840
Distinguish confirmed observations, source assertions, and analytical judgments.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:36.860
Explain confidence in plain language and use the organization's defined confidence scale

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:37.840
consistently.

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.240
Report limitations and gaps.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:43.810
Note stale records, ambiguous identities, translation issues, missing primary material,

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:47.455
possible source coordination, and areas outside authorized scope.

00:00:47.455 --> 00:00:51.475
Decision-makers need to know what is not established and what could change the conclusion.

00:00:51.475 --> 00:00:54.120
Recommendations should be lawful, proportionate, and tied to the finding.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.735
They may include internal validation, monitoring an approved public source,

00:00:57.735 --> 00:01:01.090
correcting exposed information, consulting legal or privacy staff,

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.595
or collecting a specifically authorized additional record.

00:01:04.595 --> 00:01:07.315
Control dissemination according to sensitivity and purpose.

00:01:07.315 --> 00:01:11.090
Remove irrelevant personal details and avoid unsupported accusations.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:14.310
Capture feedback: did the report answer the question, arrive in time,

00:01:14.310 --> 00:01:15.600
and support a decision?

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.215
Use that feedback to improve future requirements, collection plans, analysis,

00:01:19.215 --> 00:01:20.240
and presentation.
